## std/compressus.pengu — gzip, zlib and raw deflate with explicit ownership.
##
## `std.compressus` wraps the vendored `std_c/miniz.h` + `std_c/miniz.c`
## (miniz 3.1.2, public domain / Unlicense) and adds the one thing miniz does
## not implement: the **gzip** container (RFC 1952). The result is a small,
## dependency-free compression module that reads and writes the same bytes as
## Python's `gzip`/`zlib`, Zig's `std.compress` and Odin's `core:compress`.
##
## ## Formats
##
## | Format | Magic | Checksum | Use it for |
## |---|---|---|---|
## | `Gzip` | `1f 8b` | CRC-32 + ISIZE trailer | files (`.gz`), HTTP `Content-Encoding: gzip`, `pengu add` tarballs |
## | `Zlib` | `78 xx` | Adler-32 trailer | protocols that specify zlib (some HTTP, PNG `IDAT`) |
## | `RawDeflate` | none | none | streams that already carry framing/length (ZIP members, WebSocket permessage-deflate) |
##
## Every format is a **byte-exact** standard: gzip output opens with `gzip -d`
## and `gzip.decompress`, zlib output opens with `zlib.decompress`, and both are
## verified by `tests/compat/test_compressus_vs_python.py`.
##
## ## Quick start
##
## ```pengu
## import std.compressus
## import std.spark
##
## weave main into int:
##     var packed as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_compress with "hello", CompressionLevel.Best
##     defer banish packed
##     if not packed.is_ok:
##         calling spark.println with (calling packed.error.message)
##         return 1
##     var blob as string is packed.value          # borrowed view
##     var plain as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_decompress with blob
##     defer banish plain
##     if plain.is_ok:
##         calling spark.println with plain.value  # "hello"
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Ownership (read this once)
##
## - Every weave returns a `result`. **A `result` owns its payload.** Release
##   the whole result with `banish result`, and never `banish result.value` or
##   `result.error` separately — that frees the same buffer twice.
## - `result.value` / `result.error` are **borrowed views**. Use them while the
##   result is alive.
## - `CompressError` derives `Nexus`, so `banish` on a result whose payload is
##   an error releases the reason strings and the variant box.
## - `CompressError.message` returns an **owned** string; `banish` it.
## - The file helpers return the number of bytes written and own nothing else.
##
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_compress with data, CompressionLevel.Best
## if not r.is_ok:
##     return 1
## var out as string is r.value       # borrowed: do NOT banish
## # ... use out ...
## banish r                           # releases out and the result box
## ```
##
## ## One-shot vs file helpers
##
## The one-shot weaves (`gzip_compress`, `gzip_decompress`, ...) work on a whole
## `string` in memory. The file helpers read the complete file, call the
## one-shot weave and write the complete result; they are convenience wrappers,
## **not** a streaming API, so peak memory is roughly the sum of the input and
## the output. For files above ~100 MB, compress in chunks at the application
## level or wait for the streaming API (see `docs/COMPRESSUS.md`).
##
## ## Errors
##
## | Variant | Meaning |
## |---|---|
## | `InvalidInput` | the caller passed something impossible (a NUL in a gzip filename, `Auto` to a compressor, or an input whose output would exceed the 32-bit `string` length) |
## | `Corrupt` | the compressed bytes are malformed, truncated or fail their checksum |
## | `TrailingData` | a valid stream ended before the input did; `extra_bytes` says how many bytes are left |
## | `UnsupportedFormat` | auto-detection did not recognise the magic; `magic` is the first four bytes, little-endian |
## | `AllocationFailed` | an allocation failed |
## | `FileError` | a file could not be read or written; `reason` names the path |
## | `Internal` | an unexpected miniz status; `code` is the raw `MZ_*` value |
##
## None of these panics: invalid bytes are a normal runtime condition, so every
## weave returns `error` instead. A null `ref` passed to an internal bridge is a
## programming bug and may still crash, exactly like the rest of the stdlib.
##
## ## Complexity
##
## | Operation | Cost |
## |---|---|
## | `gzip_compress`, `zlib_compress`, `deflate_compress` | O(n) + one output allocation |
## | `gzip_decompress`, `zlib_decompress`, `inflate_decompress` | O(n) + one growable output buffer |
## | `detect_format` | O(1) |
## | `crc32`, `adler32` | O(n), no allocation |
## | file helpers | O(file size) read + the one-shot cost + O(output) write |
##
## ## Smart linking
##
## `std/compressus.d.pengu` says `link "miniz"`, so `-lminiz` reaches the linker
## **only** when `std.compressus` is imported. A program that never compresses
## neither includes `miniz_bind.h` nor links a single miniz symbol.
## `tests/build/test_smart_linking.py` proves all of that with `bundle.c`, the
## `--verbose` link line and `nm`.
##
## See `docs/COMPRESSUS.md` for the format details, the gzip framing walkthrough
## and the comparison with Python, Zig and Odin.
##
## ## Why miniz, and why not a system zlib
##
## miniz is one translation unit with no external dependency, so it builds
## identically on Linux, macOS, Windows and Emscripten and a PenguScript program
## never depends on a host `zlib` ABI (which differs between `zlib`, `zlib-ng`,
## Chromium's bundled copy and Windows' `zlib1.dll`). It is public domain, which
## keeps the toolchain license simple. Its output is standard deflate: the tests
## compare it with Python byte for byte where the standard fixes the bytes.
import std.archivum
import std.builder

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Module version
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Compressus module version.
const COMPRESSUS_VERSION as string is "2.14.0"

## Size of the fixed part of a gzip header, in bytes (RFC 1952 §2.3).
const GZIP_HEADER_SIZE as int is 10

## Size of a gzip trailer: CRC-32 and ISIZE, four bytes each (RFC 1952 §2.3.1).
const GZIP_TRAILER_SIZE as int is 8

## Smallest possible gzip stream: 10-byte header, the two-byte empty deflate
## block (`03 00`) and the 8-byte trailer. `gzip -d` accepts it.
const GZIP_MIN_SIZE as int is 20

## First gzip magic byte (`0x1f`).
const GZIP_MAGIC_0 as int is 31

## Second gzip magic byte (`0x8b`).
const GZIP_MAGIC_1 as int is 139

## The only compression method gzip defines (`CM = 8`, deflate).
const GZIP_METHOD_DEFLATE as int is 8

## `FLG` bit 2: an `FEXTRA` field follows the fixed header.
const GZIP_FLAG_FEXTRA as int is 4

## `FLG` bit 3: an `FNAME` field follows (the original file name).
const GZIP_FLAG_FNAME as int is 8

## `FLG` bit 4: an `FCOMMENT` field follows.
const GZIP_FLAG_FCOMMENT as int is 16

## `FLG` bit 1: an `FHCRC` field follows (low 16 bits of the header CRC-32).
const GZIP_FLAG_FHCRC as int is 2

## Bits 5-7 of `FLG` are reserved; RFC 1952 requires them to be zero.
const GZIP_FLAG_RESERVED as int is 224

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public types
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## How hard the compressor works.
##
## Higher levels produce smaller output and take longer. The names map to the
## zlib/miniz scale; `Default` is a concrete *6* (never miniz's `-1` sentinel,
## so two calls with the same level are byte-identical).
omen CompressionLevel:
    ## Store only (`0`). The stream is valid deflate with no compression.
    None
    ## Fastest compression (`1`). Big output, low CPU.
    Fastest
    ## Balanced default (`6`). The right choice unless you measured otherwise.
    Default
    ## Above the default (`7`). A little smaller, a little slower.
    Better
    ## Best standard compression (`9`). The zlib ceiling.
    Best
    ## miniz-specific (`10`): tries harder than `Best`. Slower, and **not**
    ## accepted by a strict zlib implementation as a *level*, although the
    ## stream it emits is still standard deflate.
    Uber

## The container format around a deflate stream.
omen CompressionFormat:
    ## RFC 1952. A 10-byte header, raw deflate and a CRC-32/ISIZE trailer.
    ## What `.gz` files, `gzip -d` and HTTP `Content-Encoding: gzip` use.
    Gzip
    ## RFC 1950. A two-byte header and a big-endian Adler-32 trailer.
    ## What `zlib.decompress` expects and what PNG `IDAT` holds.
    Zlib
    ## RFC 1951. Deflate with no header and no checksum. Use it only when the
    ## surrounding protocol already provides framing and integrity.
    RawDeflate
    ## "Let `decompress_auto` decide." **Only** valid as an input to
    ## `decompress_auto`; passing it to a compressor is `InvalidInput`.
    Auto

## What went wrong while compressing, decompressing or reading/writing a file.
##
## ## Memoria
## Derives `Nexus`, so releasing a `result` that carries an error releases the
## `reason` string. `message` returns an owned description; `banish` it.
omen CompressError derive Nexus:
    ## The caller passed something no format can represent: a NUL byte in a
    ## gzip filename, an empty filename, `CompressionFormat.Auto` to a
    ## compressor, or an input whose compressed/decompressed output would
    ## exceed the 32-bit `string` length.
    InvalidInput with reason as string
    ## The compressed bytes are malformed, truncated, or fail their checksum.
    Corrupt with reason as string
    ## A complete stream ended before the input did. `extra_bytes` is the
    ## number of bytes after the last valid member.
    TrailingData with extra_bytes as int
    ## Auto-detection did not recognise the magic. `magic` is up to four bytes,
    ## little-endian (so `1f 8b` is `0x00008b1f`).
    UnsupportedFormat with magic as u32
    ## An allocation failed. Named `AllocationFailed` (the spelling predates
    ## the 2.19 variant-namespace cleanup; kept for API compatibility).
    AllocationFailed
    ## A file could not be read or written. Named `FileError` to avoid the
    ## bare `IoError` used by `std.archivum`'s error type.
    FileError with reason as string
    ## An unexpected miniz status. `code` is the raw `MZ_*` value.
    Internal with code as int, reason as string

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Error descriptions
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

enchanting CompressError:
    ## A human-readable description of the failure.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## An **owned** string; release it with `banish`.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var e as CompressError is r.error
    ## var text as string is calling e.message
    ## calling spark.println with text
    ## banish text
    ## ```
    weave message into string:
        return judge (essence of self):
            when InvalidInput with reason -> "invalid input: {reason}"
            when Corrupt with reason -> "corrupt compressed data: {reason}"
            when TrailingData with extra_bytes -> "trailing data after the last stream: {extra_bytes} bytes"
            when UnsupportedFormat with magic -> "unsupported compression format (magic {magic})"
            when AllocationFailed -> "out of memory"
            when FileError with reason -> "I/O error: {reason}"
            when Internal with code, reason -> "internal miniz error {code}: {reason}"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private C bridges
#
# Every block below either owns a byte-level operation that the language cannot
# express without a temporary allocation per byte, or calls miniz with its real
# C types. The public logic — format detection, gzip header parsing, member
# traversal and checksum comparison — stays in PenguScript below.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Returns the byte value at `i`, or 0 when `i` is out of bounds.
##
## ## Motivo
## `(calling scrolls.substring with s, i, i + 1)` allocates a one-byte string
## for every inspected byte. Header parsing inspects a dozen bytes per member;
## `.data`/`.len` allocates nothing.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
antiquus _byte_at with s as string, i as int into int:
    r"""
if (!s.data || i < 0 || i >= s.len) return 0;
return (int)(unsigned char)s.data[i];
"""

## CRC-32 of `length` bytes starting at `offset`, continuing `seed`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing. Out-of-range slices return `seed` unchanged.
antiquus _crc32_range with data as string, offset as int, length as int, seed as u32 into u32:
    r"""
if (offset < 0 || length < 0 || offset > data.len || length > data.len - offset)
    return seed;
const unsigned char *p = (const unsigned char *)(data.data ? data.data : "");
return (uint32_t)mz_crc32((mz_ulong)seed, p + offset, (size_t)length);
"""

## Adler-32 of `length` bytes starting at `offset`, continuing `seed`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing. Out-of-range slices return `seed` unchanged.
antiquus _adler32_range with data as string, offset as int, length as int, seed as u32 into u32:
    r"""
if (offset < 0 || length < 0 || offset > data.len || length > data.len - offset)
    return seed;
const unsigned char *p = (const unsigned char *)(data.data ? data.data : "");
return (uint32_t)mz_adler32((mz_ulong)seed, p + offset, (size_t)length);
"""

## Compresses `data` as a **raw** deflate stream (RFC 1951) at `level`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `tdefl_compress_mem_to_heap` takes the flag word built from
## `(level, -15, TDEFL_DEFAULT_MAX_PROBES)`, which selects raw deflate and one
## exact-size allocation. Doing the same through the streaming API would need an
## `mz_stream` the binding deliberately does not expose.
##
## ## Memoria
## The returned `PenguString` owns a `malloc` block that miniz allocated with its
## default allocator (`malloc`), which is exactly what `banish` calls. `status`
## receives `MZ_OK` or a negative `MZ_*` code.
antiquus _deflate_raw with data as string, level as int, status as ref to int into string:
    r"""
*status = MZ_OK;
const unsigned char *in = (const unsigned char *)(data.data ? data.data : "");
size_t n = (size_t)(data.len > 0 ? data.len : 0);
int flags = (int)tdefl_create_comp_flags_from_zip_params(
    level, -MZ_DEFAULT_WINDOW_BITS, TDEFL_DEFAULT_MAX_PROBES);
size_t out_len = 0;
void *buf = tdefl_compress_mem_to_heap(in, n, &out_len, flags);
if (!buf) {
    *status = MZ_MEM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
if (out_len > (size_t)INT_MAX) {
    mz_free(buf);
    *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
PenguString s;
s.data = (char *)buf;
s.len = (int)out_len;
s.is_owned = 1;
return s;
"""

## Compresses `data` as a **zlib** stream (RFC 1950) at `level`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `mz_compress2` computes the zlib header, the deflate body and the Adler-32
## trailer in one call. Reimplementing the Adler-32 trailer here would duplicate
## a checksum miniz already emits and verifies.
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates exactly `mz_compressBound(n)` bytes with `malloc`; the returned
## string owns them. `status` receives `MZ_OK` or a negative `MZ_*` code.
antiquus _deflate_zlib with data as string, level as int, status as ref to int into string:
    r"""
*status = MZ_OK;
const unsigned char *in = (const unsigned char *)(data.data ? data.data : "");
size_t n = (size_t)(data.len > 0 ? data.len : 0);
if (n > 0xFFFFFFFFu) {
    *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
mz_ulong cap = mz_compressBound((mz_ulong)n);
if (cap == 0) cap = 128;
if (cap > (mz_ulong)INT_MAX) {
    *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
unsigned char *buf = (unsigned char *)malloc((size_t)cap);
if (!buf) {
    *status = MZ_MEM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
mz_ulong out_len = cap;
int rc = mz_compress2(buf, &out_len, in, (mz_ulong)n, level);
if (rc != MZ_OK) {
    free(buf);
    *status = rc;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
if (out_len > (mz_ulong)INT_MAX) {
    free(buf);
    *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
PenguString s;
s.data = (char *)buf;
s.len = (int)out_len;
s.is_owned = 1;
return s;
"""

## Compresses `data` as a **gzip** stream (RFC 1952) at `level`.
##
## ## Motivo
## miniz has no gzip support. This block emits the 10-byte fixed header (plus an
## `FNAME` field when `filename` is non-empty), the raw deflate body and the
## CRC-32/ISIZE trailer in **one** allocation: concatenating three PenguScript
## strings would copy the body twice and allocate two temporaries.
##
## `MTIME` is always zero, so the same input and level produce the same bytes on
## any machine and at any time. `OS` is `0xff` ("unknown"), which every reader
## accepts. `XFL` follows gzip's convention (`2` for level 9, `4` for level 1,
## `0` otherwise); no reader depends on it.
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates the exact output size with `malloc`; the returned string owns it.
## The temporary deflate block is released with `mz_free` before returning.
## `status` receives `MZ_OK` or a negative `MZ_*` code.
antiquus _gzip_compress with data as string, level as int, filename as string, status as ref to int into string:
    r"""
*status = MZ_OK;
const unsigned char *in = (const unsigned char *)(data.data ? data.data : "");
size_t n = (size_t)(data.len > 0 ? data.len : 0);
size_t name_len = (filename.data && filename.len > 0) ? (size_t)filename.len : (size_t)0;

int flags = (int)tdefl_create_comp_flags_from_zip_params(
    level, -MZ_DEFAULT_WINDOW_BITS, TDEFL_DEFAULT_MAX_PROBES);
size_t raw_len = 0;
void *raw = tdefl_compress_mem_to_heap(in, n, &raw_len, flags);
if (!raw) {
    *status = MZ_MEM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}

/* header + body + trailer; the guard keeps every size arithmetic overflow-free
 * and every length inside the int the PenguString header stores. */
size_t header_len = (size_t)10 + (name_len ? name_len + 1 : (size_t)0);
if (raw_len > (size_t)INT_MAX || header_len > (size_t)INT_MAX - raw_len - (size_t)8) {
    mz_free(raw);
    *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
size_t total = header_len + raw_len + (size_t)8;
unsigned char *out = (unsigned char *)malloc(total);
if (!out) {
    mz_free(raw);
    *status = MZ_MEM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}

size_t o = 0;
out[o++] = 0x1f;
out[o++] = 0x8b;
out[o++] = 0x08;
out[o++] = name_len ? 0x08 : 0x00; /* FLG: FNAME only */
out[o++] = 0x00; /* MTIME byte 0 */
out[o++] = 0x00; /* MTIME byte 1 */
out[o++] = 0x00; /* MTIME byte 2 */
out[o++] = 0x00; /* MTIME byte 3 */
out[o++] = (unsigned char)((level == 9) ? 2 : ((level == 1) ? 4 : 0)); /* XFL */
out[o++] = 0xff; /* OS: unknown */
if (name_len) {
    memcpy(out + o, filename.data, name_len);
    o += name_len;
    out[o++] = 0x00;
}
if (raw_len) memcpy(out + o, raw, raw_len);
o += raw_len;

uint32_t crc = (uint32_t)mz_crc32(0, in, n);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)(crc & 0xff);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)((crc >> 8) & 0xff);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)((crc >> 16) & 0xff);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)((crc >> 24) & 0xff);
uint32_t isize = (uint32_t)(n & 0xffffffffu);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)(isize & 0xff);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)((isize >> 8) & 0xff);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)((isize >> 16) & 0xff);
out[o++] = (unsigned char)((isize >> 24) & 0xff);

mz_free(raw);

PenguString s;
s.data = (char *)out;
s.len = (int)o;
s.is_owned = 1;
return s;
"""

## Inflates `data[offset..]` with `window_bits` (`15` = zlib, `-15` = raw).
##
## ## Motivo
## The size of a deflate stream's output is not stored anywhere: it must be
## discovered by inflating. This block grows the output buffer geometrically
## with `realloc` and stops on `MZ_STREAM_END`, on a hard error, or when the
## input is exhausted before the end of the stream (truncation).
##
## `consumed` receives the number of **input** bytes the stream used (the offset
## of the trailer in a gzip member). `status` receives `MZ_OK` on success or a
## negative `MZ_*` code; `MZ_BUF_ERROR` means "the input ended mid-stream".
##
## ## Memoria
## Allocates one growable buffer that the returned string owns. `data` is read
## only. The temporary `mz_stream` is ended on every path.
antiquus _inflate_at with data as string, offset as int, window_bits as int, consumed as ref to int, status as ref to int into string:
    r"""
*consumed = 0;
*status = MZ_OK;
if (offset < 0 || data.len < 0 || offset > data.len) {
    *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}
const unsigned char *base = (const unsigned char *)(data.data ? data.data : "");
size_t in_len = (size_t)(data.len - offset);
if (in_len > 0xFFFFFFFFu) {
    *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}

mz_stream stream;
memset(&stream, 0, sizeof(stream));
int rc = mz_inflateInit2(&stream, window_bits);
if (rc != MZ_OK) {
    *status = rc;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}

size_t cap = 256;
if (in_len <= ((size_t)-1 - 64) / 3) cap = in_len * 3 + 64;
if (cap < 256) cap = 256;
if (cap > (size_t)(1u << 20)) cap = (size_t)(1u << 20);
unsigned char *out = (unsigned char *)malloc(cap);
if (!out) {
    mz_inflateEnd(&stream);
    *status = MZ_MEM_ERROR;
    return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
}

stream.next_in = base + offset;
stream.avail_in = (unsigned int)in_len;

size_t used = 0;
for (;;) {
    if (used == cap) {
        /* `PenguString.len` is a 32-bit int, so a larger output cannot be
         * returned; stop before the doubling arithmetic can overflow. */
        if (cap >= (size_t)INT_MAX) {
            free(out);
            mz_inflateEnd(&stream);
            *status = MZ_PARAM_ERROR;
            return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
        }
        size_t next_cap = cap * 2;
        if (next_cap > (size_t)INT_MAX) next_cap = (size_t)INT_MAX;
        unsigned char *grown = (unsigned char *)realloc(out, next_cap);
        if (!grown) {
            free(out);
            mz_inflateEnd(&stream);
            *status = MZ_MEM_ERROR;
            return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
        }
        out = grown;
        cap = next_cap;
    }
    stream.next_out = out + used;
    stream.avail_out = (unsigned int)(cap - used);
    unsigned int before_in = stream.avail_in;
    unsigned int before_out = stream.avail_out;
    rc = mz_inflate(&stream, MZ_NO_FLUSH);
    used = cap - (size_t)stream.avail_out;
    if (rc == MZ_STREAM_END) {
        *consumed = (int)stream.total_in;
        *status = MZ_OK;
        mz_inflateEnd(&stream);
        PenguString s;
        s.data = (char *)out;
        s.len = (int)used;
        s.is_owned = 1;
        return s;
    }
    if (rc != MZ_OK && rc != MZ_BUF_ERROR) {
        free(out);
        mz_inflateEnd(&stream);
        *status = rc;
        return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
    }
    if (stream.avail_out == 0) continue;
    if (stream.avail_in == before_in && stream.avail_out == before_out) {
        free(out);
        mz_inflateEnd(&stream);
        *status = MZ_BUF_ERROR;
        return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
    }
}
"""

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Maps a `CompressionLevel` to the integer miniz expects.
##
## `Default` is **6**, not miniz's `-1` sentinel: a concrete level keeps the
## output byte-identical between calls, which `tests/stdlib/test_compressus.py`
## asserts.
weave _level_code with level as CompressionLevel into int:
    return judge level:
        when None -> 0
        when Fastest -> 1
        when Default -> 6
        when Better -> 7
        when Best -> 9
        when Uber -> 10

## Reads a little-endian 32-bit integer at `at`. Out-of-range bytes read as 0.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
weave _le32 with data as string, at as int into u32:
    var b0 as int is calling _byte_at with data, at
    var b1 as int is calling _byte_at with data, at + 1
    var b2 as int is calling _byte_at with data, at + 2
    var b3 as int is calling _byte_at with data, at + 3
    return (b0 to u32) | ((b1 to u32) << 8) | ((b2 to u32) << 16) | ((b3 to u32) << 24)

## Moves the success payload out of a `result of string to CompressError`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `result.value` is a borrowed view: releasing the result releases the string
## too. `decompress_auto` has to return the plain bytes *and* release the inner
## result's box, so it moves the payload out first and then banishes an empty
## result. Doing that from PenguScript would need a copy.
##
## ## Memoria
## Transfers ownership of the string to the caller and leaves the result box
## empty (`ok_val == NULL`, `is_ok == false`), so a later `banish` on it is a
## no-op. Returns a non-owning `""` when `r` is not a successful result.
antiquus _take_ok_string with r as ref to result of string to CompressError into string:
    r"""
if (!r || !r->is_ok || !r->ok_val) return pengu_string_from_cstr("");
PenguString out = *(PenguString *)r->ok_val;
free(r->ok_val);
r->ok_val = NULL;
r->is_ok = false;
r->err_val = NULL;
return out;
"""

## Moves the error payload out of a `result of string to CompressError`.
##
## ## Motivo
## `result.error` is a borrowed view: releasing the result frees the reason
## string it points at. Every failure path in this module has to return the
## error *and* release the inner result's box, so it moves the payload out
## first. Doing that from PenguScript would copy the struct but not the string
## it owns, leaving a dangling `reason`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Transfers ownership of the `CompressError` (including its reason string) to
## the caller and leaves the result box empty, so a later `banish` on it is a
## no-op.
antiquus _take_error with r as ref to result of string to CompressError into CompressError:
    r"""
CompressError out;
memset(&out, 0, sizeof out);
if (!r || r->is_ok || !r->err_val) return out;
out = *(CompressError *)r->err_val;
free(r->err_val);
r->err_val = NULL;
r->is_ok = true;
r->ok_val = NULL;
return out;
"""

## Maps a miniz status to a `CompressError`.
##
## `context` names the operation for the `Internal` fallback, so an unexpected
## status still says *where* it happened.
weave _error_from_status with status as int, context as string into CompressError:
    if status == -4:
        return AllocationFailed
    if status == -3:
        return with Corrupt is "{context}: data error"
    if status == -5:
        return with Corrupt is "{context}: input ended before the end of the stream"
    if status == -10000:
        return with InvalidInput is "{context}: miniz rejected an out-of-range argument"
    if status == 2:
        return with Corrupt is "{context}: stream requires a preset dictionary, which std.compressus does not support"
    return with Internal is with code is status, reason is context

## Returns the offset of the first byte after the gzip header that starts at
## `at`, or a negative code describing why the header is unusable.
##
## Codes: `-1` not gzip (bad magic), `-2` truncated header, `-3` unsupported
## compression method, `-4` reserved `FLG` bits set, `-5` `FHCRC` mismatch.
##
## The parser walks every optional field RFC 1952 defines — `FEXTRA`, `FNAME`,
## `FCOMMENT` and `FHCRC` — so a stream produced by any conforming writer
## (including one with an original filename) is accepted.
##
## ## Memoria
## Reads only; allocates nothing.
weave _gzip_header_len with data as string, at as int into int:
    var n as int is data length
    # Magic first: a short run of bytes after a complete member is trailing
    # data, not a truncated header. Only bytes that *start* with `1f 8b` can be
    # a truncated member.
    if at < 0 or at >= n:
        return -2
    if (calling _byte_at with data, at) != GZIP_MAGIC_0:
        return -1
    if at + 1 >= n:
        return -2
    if (calling _byte_at with data, at + 1) != GZIP_MAGIC_1:
        return -1
    if at + GZIP_HEADER_SIZE > n:
        return -2
    if (calling _byte_at with data, at + 2) != GZIP_METHOD_DEFLATE:
        return -3
    var flags as int is calling _byte_at with data, at + 3
    if (flags & GZIP_FLAG_RESERVED) != 0:
        return -4
    var i as int is at + GZIP_HEADER_SIZE
    if (flags & GZIP_FLAG_FEXTRA) != 0:
        if i + 2 > n:
            return -2
        var xlen as int is (calling _byte_at with data, i) + ((calling _byte_at with data, i + 1) * 256)
        set i is i + 2 + xlen
        if i > n:
            return -2
    if (flags & GZIP_FLAG_FNAME) != 0:
        while i < n:
            if (calling _byte_at with data, i) == 0:
                break
            set i is i + 1
        if i >= n:
            return -2
        set i is i + 1
    if (flags & GZIP_FLAG_FCOMMENT) != 0:
        while i < n:
            if (calling _byte_at with data, i) == 0:
                break
            set i is i + 1
        if i >= n:
            return -2
        set i is i + 1
    if (flags & GZIP_FLAG_FHCRC) != 0:
        if i + 2 > n:
            return -2
        var stored as u32 is (calling _le32 with data, i) & 65535
        var actual as u32 is (calling _crc32_range with data, at, i - at, 0) & 65535
        if stored != actual:
            return -5
        set i is i + 2
    return i - at

## Maps a `CompressionFormat` to a small integer, for comparisons.
##
## Omens are compared with `judge`, not with `is`; the code keeps
## `decompress_auto` flat instead of nesting two judges per branch.
weave _format_code with format as CompressionFormat into int:
    return judge format:
        when Gzip -> 0
        when Zlib -> 1
        when RawDeflate -> 2
        when Auto -> 3

## Maps a `_gzip_header_len` failure code to the error the public API returns.
weave _gzip_header_error with code as int, data as string, at as int, member as int into CompressError:
    if code == -1:
        if member == 0:
            return with UnsupportedFormat is calling _le32 with data, at
        return with TrailingData is with extra_bytes is ((data length) - at)
    if code == -2:
        return with Corrupt is "truncated gzip header"
    if code == -3:
        return with Corrupt is "gzip compression method is not deflate (CM != 8)"
    if code == -4:
        return with Corrupt is "gzip reserved FLG bits are set"
    return with Corrupt is "gzip header CRC16 (FHCRC) does not match"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gzip
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Compresses `data` as a gzip stream (RFC 1952), with `MTIME` zero.
##
## The output opens with `gzip -d` and with Python's `gzip.decompress`. Because
## `MTIME` is always zero, compressing the same bytes at the same level is
## deterministic.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: bytes to compress. Borrowed.
## - `level`: how hard to work. See `CompressionLevel`.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with an **owned** gzip string (release the result with `banish`), or
## `err CompressError`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_compress with "hello", CompressionLevel.Best
## defer banish r
## if r.is_ok:
##     calling archivum.write_bytes with "hello.gz", r.value
## ```
weave gzip_compress with data as string, level as CompressionLevel into result of string to CompressError:
    return calling gzip_compress_named with data, "", level

## Compresses `data` as a gzip stream that records `filename` in the `FNAME`
## header field.
##
## `FNAME` is metadata only: it is the original file name, not a path, and no
## reader is required to use it. Pass `""` for a stream with no `FNAME` field —
## that is exactly what `gzip_compress` does. A filename containing a NUL byte
## cannot be represented (the field is NUL-terminated) and is rejected with
## `InvalidInput`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: bytes to compress. Borrowed.
## - `filename`: original name to record, or `""`. Borrowed.
## - `level`: how hard to work.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with an **owned** gzip string, or `err CompressError`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_compress_named with payload, "notes.txt", CompressionLevel.Default
## defer banish r
## ```
weave gzip_compress_named with data as string, filename as string, level as CompressionLevel into result of string to CompressError:
    var name as string is filename
    if (filename length) > 0:
        var i as int is 0
        var n as int is filename length
        while i < n:
            if (calling _byte_at with filename, i) == 0:
                return calling err_of with (with InvalidInput is "gzip filename must not contain a NUL byte")
            set i is i + 1
    else:
        set name is ""
    var status as int is 0
    var packed as string is calling _gzip_compress with data, (calling _level_code with level), name, (sigil of status)
    if status != 0:
        banish packed
        return calling err_of with (calling _error_from_status with status, "gzip compression")
    return calling ok_of with packed

## Decompresses one or more concatenated gzip members.
##
## Multi-member streams (two `.gz` files concatenated with `cat`) decompress to
## the concatenation of their payloads, exactly like `gzip -d` and Python's
## `gzip.decompress`. Each member's CRC-32 and ISIZE are verified; a mismatch is
## `Corrupt`, not silently accepted.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the gzip bytes. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with the **owned** plain bytes (release the result with `banish`), or
## `err CompressError`:
## - `Corrupt` for a truncated header, a bad checksum or a truncated body;
## - `UnsupportedFormat` when `data` does not start with the gzip magic;
## - `TrailingData` when a valid member is followed by bytes that are not
##   another gzip member.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_decompress with blob
## defer banish r
## ```
weave gzip_decompress with data as string into result of string to CompressError:
    var n as int is data length
    if n < GZIP_MIN_SIZE:
        if n >= 2 and (calling _byte_at with data, 0) == GZIP_MAGIC_0 and (calling _byte_at with data, 1) == GZIP_MAGIC_1:
            return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "gzip stream is shorter than its header and trailer")
        return calling err_of with (with UnsupportedFormat is calling _le32 with data, 0)

    # A compressed member is usually smaller than its payload, so the input
    # size is a safe *lower* bound for the builder. Only multiply for small
    # inputs, where the three-times guess avoids the first reallocation without
    # risking a 32-bit overflow on a large one.
    var initial as int is n
    if n < 1048576:
        set initial is n * 3
    if initial > 67108864:
        set initial is 67108864
    var sb as builder.StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.with_capacity with initial
    defer banish sb

    var offset as int is 0
    var member as int is 0
    while offset < n:
        var header_len as int is calling _gzip_header_len with data, offset
        if header_len < 0:
            return calling err_of with (calling _gzip_header_error with header_len, data, offset, member)
        var body_at as int is offset + header_len
        var consumed as int is 0
        var status as int is 0
        var body as string is calling _inflate_at with data, body_at, -15, (sigil of consumed), (sigil of status)
        if status != 0:
            banish body
            if status == -3:
                return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "gzip member {member}: deflate data is corrupt")
            return calling err_of with (calling _error_from_status with status, "gzip member {member}")
        var trailer_at as int is body_at + consumed
        if trailer_at + GZIP_TRAILER_SIZE > n:
            banish body
            return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "gzip member {member}: truncated trailer")
        var stored_crc as u32 is calling _le32 with data, trailer_at
        var stored_size as u32 is calling _le32 with data, trailer_at + 4
        var actual_crc as u32 is calling _crc32_range with body, 0, (body length), 0
        if stored_crc != actual_crc:
            banish body
            return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "gzip member {member}: CRC-32 mismatch")
        var actual_size as u32 is (body length) to u32
        if stored_size != actual_size:
            banish body
            return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "gzip member {member}: ISIZE mismatch")
        calling sb.append with body
        banish body
        set offset is trailer_at + GZIP_TRAILER_SIZE
        set member is member + 1

    return calling ok_of with (calling sb.finish)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Zlib
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Compresses `data` as a zlib stream (RFC 1950).
##
## The output is what Python's `zlib.decompress` expects and what a zlib-aware
## HTTP server accepts. miniz computes the Adler-32 trailer.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: bytes to compress. Borrowed.
## - `level`: how hard to work.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with an **owned** zlib string, or `err CompressError`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.zlib_compress with "hello", CompressionLevel.Best
## defer banish r
## ```
weave zlib_compress with data as string, level as CompressionLevel into result of string to CompressError:
    var status as int is 0
    var packed as string is calling _deflate_zlib with data, (calling _level_code with level), (sigil of status)
    if status != 0:
        banish packed
        return calling err_of with (calling _error_from_status with status, "zlib compression")
    return calling ok_of with packed

## Decompresses a zlib stream (RFC 1950).
##
## The Adler-32 trailer is verified by miniz. Bytes after the end of the stream
## are `TrailingData`, never silently ignored.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the zlib bytes. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with the **owned** plain bytes, or `err CompressError`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.zlib_decompress with blob
## defer banish r
## ```
weave zlib_decompress with data as string into result of string to CompressError:
    if (data length) < 2:
        return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "zlib stream is shorter than its header")
    var consumed as int is 0
    var status as int is 0
    var plain as string is calling _inflate_at with data, 0, 15, (sigil of consumed), (sigil of status)
    if status != 0:
        banish plain
        if status == -3:
            return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "zlib stream is corrupt or its Adler-32 does not match")
        return calling err_of with (calling _error_from_status with status, "zlib decompression")
    if consumed != (data length):
        var extra as int is (data length) - consumed
        banish plain
        return calling err_of with (with TrailingData is with extra_bytes is extra)
    return calling ok_of with plain

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw deflate
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Compresses `data` as a **raw** deflate stream (RFC 1951).
##
## There is no header and no checksum: use it only when the surrounding protocol
## already frames the stream and protects its integrity (a ZIP member, a
## WebSocket `permessage-deflate` frame, a length-prefixed record).
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: bytes to compress. Borrowed.
## - `level`: how hard to work.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with an **owned** deflate string, or `err CompressError`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.deflate_compress with "hello", CompressionLevel.Fastest
## defer banish r
## ```
weave deflate_compress with data as string, level as CompressionLevel into result of string to CompressError:
    var status as int is 0
    var packed as string is calling _deflate_raw with data, (calling _level_code with level), (sigil of status)
    if status != 0:
        banish packed
        return calling err_of with (calling _error_from_status with status, "raw deflate compression")
    return calling ok_of with packed

## Decompresses a **raw** deflate stream (RFC 1951).
##
## Empty input is the empty string: this weaves answers "what does this stream
## decompress to", and an absent stream carries no bytes. A truncated or corrupt
## stream is `Corrupt`, and bytes after the end of the stream are
## `TrailingData`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the raw deflate bytes. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with the **owned** plain bytes, or `err CompressError`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.inflate_decompress with blob
## defer banish r
## ```
weave inflate_decompress with data as string into result of string to CompressError:
    if (data length) == 0:
        var empty as string is ""
        return calling ok_of with empty
    var consumed as int is 0
    var status as int is 0
    var plain as string is calling _inflate_at with data, 0, -15, (sigil of consumed), (sigil of status)
    if status != 0:
        banish plain
        if status == -3:
            return calling err_of with (with Corrupt is "raw deflate stream is corrupt")
        return calling err_of with (calling _error_from_status with status, "raw deflate decompression")
    if consumed != (data length):
        var extra as int is (data length) - consumed
        banish plain
        return calling err_of with (with TrailingData is with extra_bytes is extra)
    return calling ok_of with plain

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Format detection
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Detects the container format from the first bytes.
##
## Recognises the gzip magic (`1f 8b`) and a structurally valid zlib header
## (`CM = 8`, `CINFO <= 7`, `FCHECK` consistent). Raw deflate has no magic and
## is **not** detected: pass `CompressionFormat.RawDeflate` explicitly.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the bytes to inspect. Borrowed; only the first two are read.
##
## ## Retorno
## `some CompressionFormat` or `maybe none`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var f as maybe CompressionFormat is calling compressus.detect_format with blob
## if f is present:
##     calling spark.println with "known format"
## ```
weave detect_format with data as string into maybe CompressionFormat:
    var n as int is data length
    if n >= 2 and (calling _byte_at with data, 0) == GZIP_MAGIC_0 and (calling _byte_at with data, 1) == GZIP_MAGIC_1:
        var gzip as CompressionFormat is CompressionFormat.Gzip
        return some gzip
    if n >= 2:
        var cmf as int is calling _byte_at with data, 0
        var flg as int is calling _byte_at with data, 1
        if (cmf & 15) == 8 and (cmf >> 4) <= 7:
            if ((cmf * 256) + flg) % 31 == 0:
                var zlib as CompressionFormat is CompressionFormat.Zlib
                return some zlib
    return maybe none

## Packs a `string` and its format into the tuple `decompress_auto` returns.
##
## ## Memoria
## Moves `text` into the tuple; the caller owns it through the result.
weave _format_pair with text as string, format as CompressionFormat into (string, CompressionFormat):
    return text, format

## Decompresses `data` in whichever format `detect_format` recognises.
##
## Raw deflate is not auto-detected; use `inflate_decompress` when the protocol
## says the bytes are raw.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the compressed bytes. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok (plain, format)` with the owned plain bytes and the detected format, or
## `err CompressError`. An unrecognised magic is `UnsupportedFormat` with the
## first four bytes (little-endian) in `magic`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of (string, CompressionFormat) to CompressError is calling compressus.decompress_auto with blob
## defer banish r
## if r.is_ok:
##     var pair as (string, CompressionFormat) is r.value
##     var plain as string is pair.0
## ```
weave decompress_auto with data as string into result of (string, CompressionFormat) to CompressError:
    var detected as maybe CompressionFormat is calling detect_format with data
    if not (detected is present):
        banish detected
        return calling err_of with (with UnsupportedFormat is calling _le32 with data, 0)
    var format as CompressionFormat is detected.value
    banish detected
    var code as int is calling _format_code with format
    if code == 0:
        var gz as result of string to CompressError is calling gzip_decompress with data
        if gz.is_ok:
            var plain as string is calling _take_ok_string with (sigil of gz)
            banish gz
            return calling ok_of with (calling _format_pair with plain, format)
        var gz_failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of gz)
        banish gz
        return calling err_of with gz_failure
    if code == 1:
        var zr as result of string to CompressError is calling zlib_decompress with data
        if zr.is_ok:
            var plain as string is calling _take_ok_string with (sigil of zr)
            banish zr
            return calling ok_of with (calling _format_pair with plain, format)
        var zr_failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of zr)
        banish zr
        return calling err_of with zr_failure
    return calling err_of with (with UnsupportedFormat is calling _le32 with data, 0)

## Decompresses `data` as an explicit format, with `Auto` as the detecting
## choice.
##
## This is the uniform entry point for code that already knows the format (a
## protocol field, a file extension, a manifest): `Gzip`, `Zlib` and
## `RawDeflate` dispatch to the matching decompressor, and `Auto` calls
## `decompress_auto`. The returned tuple always says which decoder actually ran.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the compressed bytes. Borrowed.
## - `format`: the container, or `CompressionFormat.Auto`.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok (plain, format)` with the **owned** plain bytes, or `err CompressError`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of (string, CompressionFormat) to CompressError is calling compressus.decompress_as with blob, CompressionFormat.Auto
## defer banish r
## if r.is_ok:
##     let (plain, fmt) is r.value
## ```
weave decompress_as with data as string, format as CompressionFormat into result of (string, CompressionFormat) to CompressError:
    var code as int is calling _format_code with format
    if code == 3:
        return calling decompress_auto with data
    if code == 0:
        var gzip_result as result of string to CompressError is calling gzip_decompress with data
        if gzip_result.is_ok:
            var plain as string is calling _take_ok_string with (sigil of gzip_result)
            banish gzip_result
            return calling ok_of with (calling _format_pair with plain, format)
        var gzip_failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of gzip_result)
        banish gzip_result
        return calling err_of with gzip_failure
    if code == 1:
        var zlib_result as result of string to CompressError is calling zlib_decompress with data
        if zlib_result.is_ok:
            var plain as string is calling _take_ok_string with (sigil of zlib_result)
            banish zlib_result
            return calling ok_of with (calling _format_pair with plain, format)
        var zlib_failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of zlib_result)
        banish zlib_result
        return calling err_of with zlib_failure
    var raw_result as result of string to CompressError is calling inflate_decompress with data
    if raw_result.is_ok:
        var plain as string is calling _take_ok_string with (sigil of raw_result)
        banish raw_result
        return calling ok_of with (calling _format_pair with plain, format)
    var raw_failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of raw_result)
    banish raw_result
    return calling err_of with raw_failure

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Checksums
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## CRC-32 (ISO 3309 / ITU-T V.42) of `data`, the checksum gzip stores.
##
## `crc32("")` is `0`. The result matches Python's `zlib.crc32(data)` and
## `crc32` from `binascii`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the bytes to checksum. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## The 32-bit checksum.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var c as u32 is calling compressus.crc32 with "hello"
## ```
weave crc32 with data as string into u32:
    return calling _crc32_range with data, 0, (data length), 0

## CRC-32 of `data` continuing a previous checksum.
##
## `crc32_continue(crc32(a), b) == crc32(a + b)`, so a large file can be
## checksummed chunk by chunk without keeping it in memory. Start with `0`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `initial`: the previous checksum, or `0` to start.
## - `data`: the next bytes. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## The updated 32-bit checksum.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var c as u32 is 0
## set c is calling compressus.crc32_continue with c, chunk_a
## set c is calling compressus.crc32_continue with c, chunk_b
## ```
weave crc32_continue with initial as u32, data as string into u32:
    return calling _crc32_range with data, 0, (data length), initial

## Adler-32 (RFC 1950) of `data`, the checksum zlib stores.
##
## `adler32("")` is `1`. The result matches Python's `zlib.adler32(data)`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `data`: the bytes to checksum. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## The 32-bit checksum.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var a as u32 is calling compressus.adler32 with "hello"
## ```
weave adler32 with data as string into u32:
    return calling _adler32_range with data, 0, (data length), 1

## Adler-32 of `data` continuing a previous checksum.
##
## `adler32_continue(adler32(a), b) == adler32(a + b)`. Start with `1`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `initial`: the previous checksum, or `1` to start.
## - `data`: the next bytes. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## The updated 32-bit checksum.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var a as u32 is 1
## set a is calling compressus.adler32_continue with a, chunk
## ```
weave adler32_continue with initial as u32, data as string into u32:
    return calling _adler32_range with data, 0, (data length), initial

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File helpers
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Reads `input_path`, compresses it as gzip and writes `output_path`.
##
## The whole file is read into memory and the whole result is written at once;
## see the module note on large files.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `input_path`: file to read. Borrowed.
## - `output_path`: file to create or truncate. Borrowed.
## - `level`: how hard to work.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with the number of **compressed** bytes written, `err CompressError`
## (`FileError` when either file cannot be opened).
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of int to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_compress_file with "notes.txt", "notes.txt.gz", CompressionLevel.Best
## ```
weave gzip_compress_file with input_path as string, output_path as string, level as CompressionLevel into result of int to CompressError:
    var content as maybe string is calling archivum.read_bytes with input_path
    if not (content is present):
        banish content
        return calling err_of with (with FileError is "cannot read '{input_path}'")
    var data as string is content.value
    var packed as result of string to CompressError is calling gzip_compress with data, level
    banish content
    if not packed.is_ok:
        var failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of packed)
        banish packed
        return calling err_of with failure
    var blob as string is packed.value
    var written as bool is calling archivum.write_bytes with output_path, blob
    var size as int is blob length
    banish packed
    if not written:
        return calling err_of with (with FileError is "cannot write '{output_path}'")
    return calling ok_of with size

## Reads `input_path` as gzip and writes the plain bytes to `output_path`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `input_path`: gzip file to read. Borrowed.
## - `output_path`: file to create or truncate. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with the number of **decompressed** bytes written, or `err`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of int to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_decompress_file with "notes.txt.gz", "notes.txt"
## ```
weave gzip_decompress_file with input_path as string, output_path as string into result of int to CompressError:
    var content as maybe string is calling archivum.read_bytes with input_path
    if not (content is present):
        banish content
        return calling err_of with (with FileError is "cannot read '{input_path}'")
    var data as string is content.value
    var plain as result of string to CompressError is calling gzip_decompress with data
    banish content
    if not plain.is_ok:
        var failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of plain)
        banish plain
        return calling err_of with failure
    var plain_bytes as string is plain.value
    var written as bool is calling archivum.write_bytes with output_path, plain_bytes
    var size as int is plain_bytes length
    banish plain
    if not written:
        return calling err_of with (with FileError is "cannot write '{output_path}'")
    return calling ok_of with size

## Reads a gzip file and returns its decompressed contents.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `path`: the `.gz` file. Borrowed.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with the **owned** plain bytes, or `err`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of string to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_read_file with "notes.txt.gz"
## ```
weave gzip_read_file with path as string into result of string to CompressError:
    var content as maybe string is calling archivum.read_bytes with path
    if not (content is present):
        banish content
        return calling err_of with (with FileError is "cannot read '{path}'")
    var data as string is content.value
    var plain as result of string to CompressError is calling gzip_decompress with data
    banish content
    return plain

## Compresses `data` as gzip and writes it to `path`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `path`: file to create or truncate. Borrowed.
## - `data`: bytes to compress. Borrowed.
## - `level`: how hard to work.
##
## ## Retorno
## `ok` with nothing, or `err`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var r as result of void to CompressError is calling compressus.gzip_write_file with "notes.txt.gz", "hello", CompressionLevel.Best
## ```
weave gzip_write_file with path as string, data as string, level as CompressionLevel into result of void to CompressError:
    var packed as result of string to CompressError is calling gzip_compress with data, level
    if not packed.is_ok:
        var failure as CompressError is calling _take_error with (sigil of packed)
        banish packed
        return calling err_of with failure
    var blob as string is packed.value
    var written as bool is calling archivum.write_bytes with path, blob
    banish packed
    if not written:
        return calling err_of with (with FileError is "cannot write '{path}'")
    return calling ok_of with 0

